+### 10.4 Concrete integration register
+
+These are proposed move/binding targets for the representative cross-owner
+edges, not names of a new production capability protocol. WP-01 expands this
+register to every incoming/outgoing edge in the source ledger.
+
+| Consumer → provider | Current seam/behavior | Destination and binding owner | Compatibility proof |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Feed → Gratitude | `GratitudeFeedAdapter` reads selections YAML | Feed-owned adapter implements Feed port; injected Gratitude selections query comes from Gratitude application public facade; backend composition binds both | Identical Feed items/filter/order for fixture selections; Feed imports neither Gratitude datastore nor YAML shape |
+| Homebot → Gratitude | Injected broad service exposes `addSelections` | Homebot application receives its narrow command port; Homebot-owned bridge delegates to injected Gratitude command; backend composition binds | Same assignment effects, validation, duplicates and return behavior |
+| Family Selector / app parameter resolver → household identity | Calls `/api/v1/gratitude/bootstrap` | Identity capability owns the reusable projection/client seam; preserve old endpoint and payload, with existing selection behavior; composition supplies query to Gratitude API | Existing URL and clients remain supported; synthetic user options match exactly; no endpoint removal or new auth scope |
+| Installed screens → Piano/School/Health | Built-ins import concrete components | `frontend/src/composition/screens/` registers each owner's public web export; screen-host registry stays generic | Same widget IDs/context/props; generic host with fake widget has no application import |
+| Piano → gaming | Rule/authority helpers plus challenge provider | Piano-owned challenge adapter and presenters; gaming owns protocol/authority; outer product composition supplies provider | Seed/revision/score, MIDI evidence, budget and completion parity; no gaming→Piano implementation import |
+| School → Piano/Fitness | Lifecycle consumes learning/challenge/session evidence | School-owned port/translation bridge; backend composition supplies peer public queries/commands | Same assignment completion/evidence and unavailable dependency behavior as baseline |
+| Product renderer → physical printer | Gratitude-specific `TemporaryImagePrintGateway` implements its port | `modules/gratitude/server/adapters/`; generic fleet/transport under print-output; composition injects renderer and transport separately | Unchanged rendered fixture and print calls; renderer imports neither port nor adapter |
+| Media/Piano/Fitness/School → Player | Main component plus deep controller/helper imports | Playback publishes minimal supported web subentries; each product keeps host policy wrapper | Consumer-specific playback/control/clear/completion/resume tests, including current callback defaults |
+| Admin → product settings | Hardcoded editor imports/config operations | Product owns editor/operations; Admin shell uses public entries selected in composition | Same editor route/order/config read-write behavior and permissions |
+
+The old Gratitude bootstrap URL is an intentional external contract, not a
+permitted permanent private-code dependency. Preserving that URL can mean the
+router delegates to an injected identity query; it does not require a new public
+identity endpoint. The initial refactor preserves the projection exactly,
+including current household selection behavior, rather than silently fixing it.
+
